# ============================================================================
#  CODEOWNERS — field stewards
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  When someone opens a pull request touching a file listed here, GitHub
#  automatically requests a review from that file's owner(s). This is how we
#  give domain experts stewardship over the field(s) they know: they review the
#  data changes in their area for accuracy.
#
#  Format:  <path>   @github-handle [@another-handle ...]
#  Later matches win, so the field-specific lines below override the defaults.
#
#  To become a field steward: open a PR adding your handle next to a field and
#  introduce yourself (see CONTRIBUTING.md → Governance & credit). Remove the
#  leading "# " to activate a line once an owner exists.
#
#  NOTE: every handle here must have write/triage access to the repo, or GitHub
#  will silently ignore it. Until you add real owners, keep the lines commented.
# ============================================================================

# --- Default: everything is owned by the maintainers -------------------------
# * @your-handle

# --- Engine & tooling (code review, not data review) -------------------------
# /js/layout.js         @your-handle
# /js/graph.js          @your-handle
# /js/app.js            @your-handle
# /scripts/             @your-handle
# /.github/             @your-handle

# --- Field data: one line per discipline; assign the expert who stewards it --
